null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0075083789297948345,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":37.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0037655364901281415,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":15.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0017526338445388312,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":52.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02929132979428404,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":51.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.19476,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bridgewater Bancshares, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Bridgewater Bank that provides banking products and services in the United States. The company provides commercial loans, including loans secured by nonfarm, nonresidential properties, multifamily residential properties, and nonowner occupied single family residential properties; construction, land development, and commercial and industrial loans; commercial real estate loans, such as owner and nonowner occupied properties; single family residential construction, land development, finished lots and raw land, and commercial and multifamily construction loans, as well as paycheck protection program loans. It offers deposit products, including savings and money market accounts, demand deposits, time and brokered deposits, and interest and noninterest bearing transaction accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. In addition, the company offers online, mobile, and direct banking services. The company was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Saint Louis Park, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gerald John Baack | CEO, Founder & Non Independent Executive Chairman | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 360 people. Revenue per employee of $398K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $61K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Bridgewater Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $582M market cap on $143M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $22M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.60\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head-To-Head Analysis: Bridgewater Bancshares (BWB) versus Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/head-to-head-analysis-bridgewater-bancshares-bwb-versus-its-competitors.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794395726.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"t